      "description": "Kalaupapa is on an isolated area of the island of Molokai.  This is the location of Hawaii's only leprosy colony first established as a prison in 1866, but now a refuge and national park.  There are no patients remaining with active leprosy, but some of the older Hawaii residents, now cured, still live there.  It is a beautiful village, but very difficult to reach - mainly by mule or hiking down some of the steepest cliffs in the world, or reaching it by small airplane.",
